<title>RUSSIA: Volga-Dnepr delivers cargo for Star Wars film.</title>
<headline>Volga-Dnepr delivers cargo for Star Wars film.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian cargo airline AO Volga-Dnepr has delivered from London to Tunisia 100 tonnes of equipment for shooting George Lucas' new Star Wars film, a company spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;An Antonov An-124 freighter delivered a cargo earlier this week, including a mock spacecraft and other equipment for shooting the film,&quot; the spokesman told Reuters. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>Ulyanovsk-based Volga-Dnepr currently operates 12 cargo planes -- seven An-124s, three Ilyushin Il-76TDs, one An-12 and one An-32. It uses a Yakovlev Yak-40 jet for regular passenger flights between Ulyanovsk and Moscow.</p>
<p>--Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
